{"reference":"1 Kings 3","book":"1 Kings","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Solomon’s discernment","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Solomon asks for a listening heart so that he can judge the people with discernment. The later dispute between the two women over the living child illustrates that gift: his judgment distinguishes the child’s mother and shows the wisdom he had asked to receive.","verse_refs":["1 Kings 3:4-28"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_003_2a9ed6993644f6ffa7da9973"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}